Dear Hiring Team,

I am pleased to apply for the Software Engineer I position with LexisNexis Legal & Professional. I bring more than three years of software engineering experience, an MS in Computer Science with a 4.0 GPA, and hands-on success implementing maintainable system components in Java/J2EE, JavaScript/TypeScript, Python, and SQL. The opportunity to apply that foundation to technology that improves customers' work and advances the rule of law is especially meaningful to me.

At Sperse, I translate detailed specifications into production CRM components serving more than 10,000 users across 40+ specialized agents. I also built a Codex and Bitbucket MCP code-review pipeline that accelerates testing, debugging, documentation, and triage for 25–30 pull requests per week. That work reflects the AI-first development workflow LexisNexis describes: using AI-assisted and agentic development tools while reviewing AI-generated code for correctness, quality, security, and maintainability. My test-driven FastMCP service further exposed 160+ typed, access-controlled backend actions, giving me practical experience completing bug fixes, resolving technical issues, and collaborating through code reviews.

Previously at Qualitest, I developed a Java/J2EE and Spring Boot data storage subsystem backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, with file operations spanning Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I used SQL data manipulation and data modeling principles—including window functions, materialized views, and indexes—to reduce query latency, then communicated the results through JavaScript and HTML React visualizations. Working with engineers and business stakeholders in Agile development environments also required writing detailed specifications, following coding best practices, and improving reliability across more than 100,000 weekly AWS Step Functions executions.

LexisNexis's emphasis on innovation and collaboration across boundaries matches how I work: learning emerging technologies quickly, validating their output rigorously, and turning them into reliable systems with teammates and stakeholders. I would welcome the opportunity to help develop and improve the software that combines legal and business information with analytics and technology, strengthening the tools customers use to make decisions and supporting LexisNexis's mission to advance the rule of law.

I would value the chance to discuss my interest in the Software Engineer I role. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

